Chapter 10-34: "When the Time Comes"

---

—To be honest, what we know about the "Beloved Children" is frustratingly little.

They are a group directly under the Lust Sin Archbishop, Capella Emerada Lugunica, and apparently they themselves have no awareness of belonging to the Witch Cult—they simply recognize themselves as Capella's subordinates. Those currently carrying out the "Body Swapping Dolls" across the Kingdom of Lugunica are in a different position entirely; among Capella's subordinates, only a select few are counted as "Beloved Children."

And the condition for being chosen as one of those select "Beloved Children" is—

"—Having a special power that no one else possesses. Mama... that person called it the children's 'talent.' Because a special person deserves special children..."

"The more I hear, the more it sounds like garbage logic, and the fact that my interpretation matches so perfectly is terrifying. So, 'White Sheep'-chan, what's your basis for saying the 'Beloved Children' have arrived—and that there are two or more?"

"It's an inference from what's happening. The fact that we couldn't control our hearts, and the fact that sound disappeared... these are clearly occurring separately."

"Is there no possibility of one person having multiple powers—a multi-ability user?"

"I can't say with absolute certainty that there isn't, but I think it's more likely that 'Beloved Children' don't act alone. —They're made to watch each other, so they can't run away."

Even the answer to that question was smeared with Capella's ugliness, making him feel sick.

But Subaru himself thought that possibility was low. After all, when he heard "multiple abilities," the only ones who came to mind were Reinhardt and the Gluttony Sin Archbishop. Both were outliers—existences at the extremes of good and evil—and it was hard to imagine there being many like them.

One ability per person—just as with Divine Protections and Authorities, he decided to keep that in mind for now.

"If that's the case, the question of what I am starts strangling me, but that's fine. 'White Sheep'-chan, do you have any idea which 'Beloved Children' have arrived?"

"I'm sorry. Actually, even among 'Beloved Children,' we barely know each other... I only know an older woman who told me herself that she has a body that's very hard to kill."

"Hard to kill... well, that's certainly an ability of sorts. But for a hint about the current situation... that's right! If 'White Sheep'-chan is also a 'Beloved Child,' then you should have a special trick too—"

"—!"

In front of Subaru, who had thought maybe there was a breakthrough there, 'White Sheep' gasped. Seeing her round eyes tremble and her cheeks stiffen, Subaru realized he had chosen the wrong topic.

She doesn't think well of her own ability. That was only natural. Because of that power, she was fixated on by Capella, and even now she's forced into a position she doesn't want.

"Um, 'Grey Star'-san, I..."

"No, sorry, you don't have to say it if you don't want to. —There are still moves we can make."

Shaking his head at her hoarse voice, Subaru looked behind him at the corridor crushed into silence. Beyond that rubble should be Beatrice—they'd been separated from her and the others, but—

"Deep breath... and focus! —'Cor Leonis'!"

Exhaling the breath he'd taken, Subaru concentrated his awareness in his chest and activated the Authority of Greed—'Cor Leonis,' which identifies the position of allies and perceives their existence. Ideally, he'd be able to sense even Emilia and the others who were far away, but that was too much to hope for with Subaru's ability.

So for now, he'd settle for just the positions of allies within the Kugelsschreiber Castle—

"—Beako and 'Black Dog' are together. Moving alone is Krusch-san, and far away, two people together must be Russell-san and the others. The rest is..."

From the approximate distance and movement, and the color of the light he could sense as allies' presence, he could confirm the positional relationships and safety of Beatrice and the others in the castle.

And so, stacking up confirmations of each person's safety and relief—he found it.

"—Ferris."

Separated from Subaru and everyone else, isolated alone at a point far removed, he definitely sensed Ferris's presence. It was a weak, frail light, but—

"There, there he is! It's Ferris! That guy, that guy's alive!"

"Eh, that's really good news, but how does 'Grey Star'-san know that...?"

"Actually, I have a sensor-like power that lets me sense allies' positions! So when I tried to confirm everyone's location, Ferris was there too. That guy's safe... no, whether he's safe is questionable. The response is pretty weak. But he's alive. If he's alive... we can regroup!"

At that glimmer of hope, Subaru clenched his hands so hard his nails dug into his palms.

At the 'Return by Death' restart point, Ferris had already been taken away from Subaru's group in silence. In the worst case, the restart point itself could have already been too late.

That possibility always existed. And Subaru couldn't bear it.

"But that's not it. That's not it... Ferris is... below? Damn, I should have had Beako draw me a map of the castle! Anyway, I need to go save him right now—"

"Please calm down, 'Grey Star'-san! We can't do it alone!"

'White Sheep' spread both arms, blocking Subaru who looked about to dash off at any moment toward Ferris's response, whose safety was uncertain. She looked straight at Subaru, who was stumbling forward, and said:

"I believe you're not lying. But please, calm down. Without 'Black Dog' or 'Jade Beauty,' if we face the enemy, we'll just be defeated."

"That's... yeah, damn, you're right! I got heated and couldn't see again...!"

'White Sheep' poured the water of words on Subaru, whose vision had narrowed from impatience. That cleared his sight, but the size of the problem hadn't changed. Only the order of dealing with it changed.

"'White Sheep'-chan, can you fight? I have some cunning and a whip."

"I-I have staff techniques and some magic."

"With this hand, fighting would be reckless... then let's head to where Beako and 'Black Dog' are, since they haven't moved. We won't be able to catch up to Krusch-san who's fast on her feet."

"—Understood. Um, you can tell the location with your power, right, 'Grey Star'-san?"

"Yeah, let's go! I don't know the way, but it's this way!"

Without disturbing his concentration, maintaining 'Cor Leonis,' he began running while leading 'White Sheep.'

Ferris's safety was still worrying, but he had no choice but to believe this was the best move now. Regroup with Beatrice and the others quickly, heal 'Black Dog,' and head to rescue Ferris. If possible, he wanted to pick up Krusch and Russell and the others too, and have everyone go together.

Of course, if too many people clustered together, there was a risk they couldn't counter that phenomenon called emotional 'Collapse,' so whether that was truly the best was questionable, but—

"—?"

As he ran thinking this, Subaru furrowed his brow at a sudden sense of discomfort.

In the unfamiliar castle, detouring around broken walls and corridors with missing floors, Subaru should be running the shortest possible route toward the light of Beatrice and the others he could sense. Of course, he was moving while staying alert that encountering the enemy along the way would be the worst.

But—

"Um, 'Grey Star'-san... there's something hard to say."

"...Don't say it. No, actually say it. I want to face reality too."

To 'White Sheep,' who brought it up hesitantly, Subaru ordered with a bitter expression.

Receiving that, 'White Sheep' looked around and stiffened her body slightly—

"—We passed through here once already. We're going in circles around the same place."

"I knew it! I thought it was obvious too. That broken pillar, I saw it earlier."

Turning left at the T-junction at the dead end, a broken pillar crushed the corridor. There were many similar scenes, but this was definitely the same one. —Because the distance to Beatrice, whom they should be heading straight toward, hadn't closed at all.

"Don't tell me, not just 'Silence' that erases sound and 'Collapse' that amplifies emotions, but also 'Lost Child' that makes people get lost? Don't tell me all the 'Beloved Children' are here...!"

It was a statement made on momentum, but since all the Sin Archbishops had gathered in Pristella before, it wasn't something he could laugh off as a joke. But if by some chance that were true, compared to then, their allies' fighting strength was far too weak. At least, he'd like to trade Rachins for Reinhardt.

"I'd also swap for Garfiel, and bring Julius and Roswaal too. Or better yet, call Sechs as a helper and flip the table—"

"I-I think it's unlikely that all 'Beloved Children' are out... but if the enemy intends to settle things here, it's not impossible. Um, there's also the hidden door leading to the research room, so the possibility that we're being made to get lost by this castle's mechanisms isn't zero..."

"If that's the case, then Beako prioritizing reminiscing over explaining the castle's security is too much of a fielders' choice. Also, there are two things bothering me. Both about Krusch-san."

Subaru held up two fingers, and 'White Sheep' blinked, saying "'Jade Beauty'-san?"

When he heard "corridor of lost wandering," the first thing Subaru remembered was the prank Beatrice had once set up at Roswaal's mansion—a corridor that looped infinitely. That was a kind of illusion, but Krusch's 'Dragon's Eye' should have been able to see through it at a glance.

In addition, after clashing with 'Black Dog' due to the discord brought by 'Collapse' and cutting him down, Krusch said she'd look for Ferris and ran off in her original direction. —That was also strange.

"If you're looking for Ferris, you should go back the way you came. He was taken by 'Silence' because he was walking at the very back... and indeed, Ferris is underground, in that direction, I think."

Though it was hard to grasp the positional relationship precisely, 'Cor Leonis' said Ferris's current location was underground, closer to the entrance than where Subaru and the others were, heading deeper into the castle.

Even Krusch, even with her blood up from 'Collapse,' should have understood that much.

"But she ran forward. There was nothing off about Krusch-san. If the same kind of thing is happening to us now..."

They think they're heading toward their destination, but they can't get closer to it at all. —They're being warped. Their sense of distance and direction. They're running on the rail next to the rail they think they're on.

Because of that, Subaru and the others—no, probably none of their allies will reach their destination.

"...Hey, this is quietly bad."

He'd inferred the opponent's abilities from what had happened, but each one individually didn't seem like much of a threat—yet depending on the situation and how they were combined, could they pursue harassment this thoroughly?

As expected of Capella's children—when it came to making people miserable, they were a stellar lineup.

"Ah, 'White Sheep'-chan is different, she's the original, separate. 'Black Dog' guy, I'll reserve judgment on him..."

"—Maybe we should reconsider our premise."

"Eh?"

"Even if we keep aimlessly trying to regroup, we definitely won't reach them. Somewhere along the way, we need to make our own move too... 'Grey Star'-san."

'White Sheep,' who had been thinking with her hand to her mouth, suddenly raised her face. When Subaru said "Yes!" in surprise at her intensity, she indicated the entire castle with both hands and said:

"You can sense allies' locations, right? Anyone is fine. Try pointing at them."

"—. Got it. That way, Beako is there. 'Black Dog' too."

Following 'White Sheep's' instruction, wondering if she had some idea, he pointed in the direction of the light he sensed. Confirming that direction, 'White Sheep' nodded "Understood," and then:

"Then let's try heading that way. Ready, set—"

"Wha—when you say it suddenly like that—huh?"

Urged on by 'White Sheep' without warning, Subaru hurriedly took a step. —Now, toward the opposite direction from where Beatrice was, whom he was pointing at.

At his own movements, which were undeniably abnormal, he couldn't help but swallow hard.

"Don't tell me my brain's wiring is being messed with like this? If so..."

"—No, this time try closing your eyes. Then, try walking toward where you sense 'Librarian'-san's presence."

"—? My eyes? But I don't think that would change anything..."

Though he couldn't imagine it would, he closed his eyes and focused on 'Cor Leonis.' Unchanged, toward Beatrice beside 'Black Dog,' he moved his feet through the darkness behind his eyelids—

"—Just as I thought."

At 'White Sheep's' voice, he opened his eyes and confirmed his position.

He'd moved only a single step, but that step, unlike the earlier one that went in the wrong direction, had properly advanced toward where he sensed Beatrice.

"W-what was different? Don't tell me it's a type of illusion that enters through the eyes..."

"Probably, 'Grey Star'-san's power became higher output than the current 'Lost Child.' The power relationships between Divine Protections, Demon Eyes, and abilities are extremely strict..."

"Ability... I see, 'Cor Leonis' is an Authority."

If he could surpass it through the power relationship between abilities, then an Authority could overwrite the effect of the opponent's power.

If he closed his eyes and focused one hundred percent on 'Cor Leonis,' he could break through the obstacle preventing him from reaching his destination caused by 'Lost Child'—

"Great achievement, 'White Sheep'-chan! This'll work! Alright, now for real, follow me!"

"Ah, please wait! It seems like it'll work, but..."

"No, we've already lost a lot of time! We'll make it up from here—bwonlehf!"

Following the breakthrough he'd finally found, Subaru tried to bravely chase Beatrice's light with his eyes closed—his body collided head-on with a hard wall, and he tumbled spectacularly into the corridor.

He'd smashed his forehead and nose hard. When he tumbled, he failed to break his fall.

"Gaaah... damn, of course... walls and pillars don't disappear..."

"S-sorry, I couldn't make it in time!"

"N-no, it's not your fault. It's mine. My head's fault. ...But damn, what do we do?"

Even though they'd finally found a way not to be misled by 'Lost Child,' the fact remained that this was Ballpoint Castle full of dead ends and detours. To avoid repeating the current tragedy, Subaru with his eyes closed would have to proceed while nervously checking walls and floors, but—

"I might be able to help a little by guiding you about the corridor's condition from behind..."

"But that still means we'll be slow, huh. And on top of that, because we've been misled so much, the distance to Beako and the others has grown. Getting there is..."

"—Not realistic right now, is it?"

'White Sheep,' who had caught up with the conclusion of Subaru's train of thought, asked that, and he nodded.

The urgent need to regroup with Beatrice and the others hadn't changed, but even using the method they'd found, they couldn't predict how long it would take to regroup.

And while they were doing that—

"—Krusch-san's movement changed. This, she's fighting...!"

Krusch, who had been moving quickly through the castle, stopped and began movements other than running at that location. From the changes in the light and heat he sensed, Subaru felt the signs of her fighting. Moreover, he could even guess who she was fighting.

Because—

"It's not that far, yet I can't hear the sounds of fighting."

Facing the direction where he sensed Krusch, Subaru felt an overly quiet atmosphere like that of a Japanese garden coming from there. —Without a doubt, Krusch was fighting 'Silence.'

Unconsciously, Subaru put his hand to his stomach, remembering the wide blade that had skewered him from behind. It wasn't hard to imagine that was 'Silence's' weapon.

"—"

In that instant, two thoughts sparked in Subaru's mind.

The proper thought: if Krusch is fighting the enemy, they should rush to her aid.

The humiliating thought: if the opponent is 'Silence,' Subaru and the others' presence would be a hindrance.

"—With 'Silence' as the opponent, we can't coordinate either."

If they were in a relationship where they could coordinate without words, through unspoken understanding, it would be different, but unfortunately, Subaru and Krusch didn't have that level of relationship, and their abilities weren't even close to equal to begin with.

Therefore, a careless reunion could itself be an act that benefits the enemy. —That's what made Subaru hesitate to regroup with Krusch at this moment.

And there was one more reason Subaru thought this way—

"—From here, Ferris is close."

Yes, that's right. At a realistic distance they could reach with Subaru's guidance using 'Cor Leonis' responses with his eyes closed, both Krusch and Ferris were there.

Krusch is engaged with the enemy, Ferris is either captured by the enemy or left incapacitated by wounds. Either way, both are in different predicaments.

However, if there was something to consider, it was that right now, 'Silence' wasn't near Ferris.

If 'Silence' is fully occupied with Krusch, then now—

"And if we have Ferris, the safety of our allies goes up dramatically. If we can regroup with 'Black Dog,' he can return to the front lines immediately. So..."

"So you're saying we should go save 'Blue Serpent'-san."

Receiving Subaru's theoretical armament, 'White Sheep' tightened her lips on her lovely face and pondered.

He understood her concern. No matter what, Subaru and 'White Sheep' were non-combatants, and even if they recklessly saved Ferris, it would just mean three non-combatants, far from a boost in fighting power. Even without 'Silence,' at minimum 'Collapse' and 'Lost Child' remained. In the end, they hadn't found any real countermeasure against them.

If avoiding risk, they should aim to regroup with Beatrice and the others even if it took time.

"—But on a path where you don't take a single risk, you can't obtain a single thing you want."

"'Grey Star'-san..."

"Honestly, I'm aware I'm asking for something pretty difficult. 'White Sheep'-chan has her own reasons for being in 'Six Tongues' that she has to accomplish. I'm sure you can't afford to fail, right? But... but!"

If you fear failure and keep hesitating, you won't be able to step forward even at the crucial moment.

Subaru had learned that through countless failures, and each time, he'd been beaten down by regret and remorse that felt like his soul being torn apart.

Because he was that kind of person, he could say it. —The time that matters will definitely come.

"Here, let's show our resolve. So we can face our precious comrades."

"—I will."

He didn't know if this was the best choice. Whether it was a choice worth dragging people into the same deadly situation.

But he knew that if he didn't choose this now, he would regret it to death.

And to Subaru's words, 'White Sheep' nodded back with a determined expression—

"I'll choose too. —So I can face that person."

△▼△▼△▼△

—Always, always always, always always always, he thinks.

Why am I so useless? Why am I so pathetic? Why am I so defective?

Why—only the voice tormenting himself doesn't disappear. —That too was a kind of masturbation.

"Really, I hate myself..."

The moment he woke up and understood his situation, he wanted to die of shame. Of course, he couldn't die that way. By any method, this life couldn't be easily taken.

That was Felix Argyle's special skill—so wretched it made him want to curse.

"—Hey, I'm always, always thinking about this, will you listen?"

Suddenly, while he was cursing himself, such a shrill voice came from directly in front of him. Glancing over, standing there was a woman with long hair wearing a black hat and black dress.

She pressed both hands together in front of her face, looked at Felix with dreamy eyes, and said:

"Don't you think the right hand and left hand were born to snuggle together perfectly like this, like destined existences? Right foot and left foot are different. Because they never stick together like this, right? So feet don't love each other... but right hand and left hand!"

"—"

"No, wait a moment? If you look more closely, not just the hands, but the fingers overlap perfectly too, right? Thumb, index finger, middle finger! Even the pinky! And it's still just the pinky!"

Whether it was that fun, the woman with flushed cheeks was writhing and squealing. Her attitude was so irritating that he wanted to throw cold water on it.

"...Some people are born without one hand. People who lose hands or fingers to injuries too."

"—"

It was an extreme argument, but the one who'd thrown out an extreme argument that was already finished to begin with was the woman.

Maybe he'd touch a nerve and get hurt. Even if that happened, he had a slightly reckless feeling that it would be fine if he could get her attention.

However—

"...That's the best."

Instead of getting angry, the woman exhaled hotly with rapture, and her eyes looking at Felix moistened. Then she raised both hands above her head and began spinning around on the spot,

"Because love burns brighter the higher the obstacles! Class differences! Species differences! Age, gender, ethics, morality, law! All all of them are detonators to make love burn brighter! And what's the greatest obstacle... fufu, ufufu, do you un-der-stand?"

"—"

He regretted throwing cold water on her in an instant.

It was a vein that wouldn't yield anything worthwhile no matter how much you dug. Or rather, he'd struck a spring that only gushed poison. —Actually, the word poison wasn't far off at all.

"...You've been doing something to me all along, haven't you? What is this?"

"Something... you mean your arm? If that's it, it wasn't me, it was Reborn who did it. Really, what a brute. For that Reborn, I think someone older and more composed, or conversely a younger person who needs more care, would suit him! How about it!?"

"Not the arm. You're trying to mess with my head."

"Ah, that? Fufu, don't misunderstand. I'm not doing it just to you. To everyone in this castle... ah! Could it be, you wanted to be specially treated? But if so, does that mean you like me? Me too!"

To the woman who proclaimed love with dreamy eyes, Felix abandoned hope for a proper conversation.

Even without that, no fool would reveal their hand to the enemy. As a matter of fact, Felix felt external interference in his body and his body continuously healing it.

The special technique woven into Felix's body was magic that continuously maintained its optimal state through sustained activation. With this, Felix could respond to abnormalities through changes in his body and od, even abnormalities he wasn't aware of, and recover.

Now too, he was apparently continuously healing the strange power the woman was trying to inflict on him.

However, this power also had a flaw. —Felix's own physical fragility.

"—"

Ignoring the writhing woman, the surroundings were indeed inside Kugelsschreiber Castle, but it was an unfamiliar space. It looked like a landing such as those found in castles and mansions, but there wasn't a single window in the high walls. Probably underground.

In that underground, Felix was a captive. —With both arms raised above his head, literally skewered, pinned to the wall.

"Frustrating, but a hundred-point finishing move..."

As mentioned, Felix's body continuously recovered to perfect condition, but as expected, with his body pierced by a blade, there was no way to heal the wound without dealing with the blade.

And Felix, hung with his arms skewered, didn't possess the physical ability to pull it out and gain freedom.

Because of that, he could only continue in this spectacle-like state—

"Don't make that face, Felix. It ruins your cute face, you know? Besides, besides? I think this isn't a bad story for you either."

"Huh? Why?"

"Actually, right now, it's in a state where people have a very hard time getting here! Everyone has no choice but to take a 'detour,' and some people along the way must get discouraged or cry. But but, if someone overcomes such obstacles and reaches here... that's your destined partner! This 'Ring Finger' Lycoris guarantees it! Burning love will envelop you!"

Because he reflexively responded to a conversation he had no intention of engaging in, he ended up being forced to listen to worthless delusions, and what he gained was about the woman's name—Lycoris.

On top of that, what Lycoris said was hope was unmistakably Felix's despair.

"...A knight as a hostage, the worst."

Even if he had no knightly ability and it was just a decorative title, an existence in a position to protect others waiting for someone to save them was nothing but a nightmare. Especially if it would result in dragging down the person he absolutely didn't want to drag down.

And for Felix, the most unbearable thing was—

"—If it were Reinhardt coming, I wouldn't mind at all."

He wanted to say it in a dying voice, but Felix's throat and tongue were in perfect condition, so it didn't come out that way. It was because he'd made them that way with magic.

Whether she knew that or not, the other party laughed softly with a "ha" like letting out breath,

"You look way more alive than you appear, Ferris."

Whether on purpose or because her mood was elevated, the boy with glaring eyes appeared in the landing as if dancing, making unnecessarily loud footsteps. Looking at Felix pinned to the far wall of the wide space from the underground entrance, the boy—Natsuki Subaru—glared at Lycoris standing at the feet of the hanging Felix.

And with sharp eyes still, he pointed at her with a snap,

"Hyahha! Finally we meet, 'Beloved Children'! I've been waiting impatiently for the day I could see your faces!"

"—"

At Subaru, who widened his eyes sharply and cracked his voice with spirit, Felix furrowed his brow. Even for his usual bravado, it was a bit excessive.

"...This is that kind of thing, huh."

If what was happening to Subaru now and what Felix's body was continuously healing were caused by the same factor, he could guess what Lycoris was doing.

She was scattering it. —A 'poison' in the air that drives people mad.

Lycoris, displaying her literally poisonous woman nature, hugged herself as if terrified by Subaru's outburst,

"Just as I thought! Just as I thought! Natsuki loved Felix! Otherwise, he couldn't have overcome Tornel's 'Detour' to get here! Just as I thought, just as I hoped, just as I wished, just as I dreamed, just as just as just as just as precious—!!"

While stomping her feet pat-pat on the spot, Lycoris writhed with joy beyond limits.

Subaru, seeing it for the first time, didn't hide his revulsion and readied his whip. He seemed prepared to exchange blows with Lycoris, but—

"...Where's Beatrice-chan?"

"Beako and I are acting separately! It's not just Beako either! But don't worry, you're not alone! Me neither! I have reliable comrades! First, the whip!"

"The whip! What are you planning to use it for!? Is that also love!? Can I watch from the side? Or should I join too? Is that love? If it's love, I'm fine with it too!"

"Also courage! When it comes down to it, this is what I rely on! Also, I have a trump card—"

He probably wanted to say "there is one."

In the nightmare-like scene of Subaru and Lycoris making noise together, Felix was even starting to doubt whether this was reality.

That's why. —He couldn't catch up with understanding what happened the next moment.

"—If the trump card is me, then I'm sorry."

Suddenly, a figure appeared behind Subaru, who was shouting loudly, and clung to his body. —No, wrong. It only looked like clinging. The reality was different. She'd slammed into him with her whole body.

Why? Because that way, it wouldn't come out. Because it would sink in deep. —Because the sharp knife she held with both hands at hip level could skillfully gouge the vital spot in Subaru's side.

"Shiro, hitsuji, chan...?"

Looking at the knife stuck in his side and the person gripping it, Subaru called that name, that nickname. Because neither Subaru nor Felix knew her name.

"Bu" —spilling overflowing blood from his mouth, Subaru fell to his knees on the spot. At Subaru kneeling there, she—'White Sheep'—looked down with eyes colder than anything he'd ever seen, and said:

"—I chose. To fulfill my wish too."
